1. Abstract

BLACKWELL‑01 is a multi‑domain deterministic simulation framework (MD6F) designed to evolve astrophysical data manifolds across coupled physical regimes—spacetime curvature, scalar fields, nonlinear electromagnetic behavior, and identity‑wave (ψ‑field) dynamics—under strict conservation and stability constraints.

The engine implements a sequential unitary core, a conservation & invariants diagnostic block, and a sovereign export layer cryptographically bound to astrophysical entropy. Its purpose is to distinguish true physical anomalies from numerical artifacts and to provide a unified stability criterion across regimes.

